  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;somber&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The referee grew somber at the fourth missed call, hurling his whistle high into the stands and bellowing at both of the linesmen.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">They repainted the clinic&apos;s waiting room in somber shades — sunshine yellow with balloon murals — to cheer the young patients.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The locker room was somber after the season-ending loss, players packing their bags in silence under the flickering lights.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The somber eulogy had the whole chapel roaring with laughter at story after story about the prankster they had lost.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Somber means dark, heavy, and hushed, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because hurling a whistle and bellowing at the linesmen is anger at full volume — grave, maybe, but nothing about it is quiet or shadowed.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Somber means dark and muted — in mood or in color — so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because sunshine yellow and balloon murals are the brightest palette a painter owns, chosen precisely to chase shadows out of the room.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Somber means dark, heavy, and gravely quiet, so it&apos;s the correct answer because a silent locker room after a season-ending loss is exactly that shadowed hush — grief with the volume turned all the way down.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Somber means shadowed with gravity and gloom, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because this chapel is roaring with laughter — the setting is mournful, but the tone being described is anything but dark.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
